# Rocdown: Document Language & Static Site Generator

Rocdown is a Markdown-first document language, static site compiler, and interactive documentation toolchain built on Roc and Rust.

---

## Core Capabilities

### ⚡ Author in Markdown
Write documentation prose, headings, lists, tables, callouts, and code blocks using standard CommonMark and GitHub Flavored Markdown syntax.

### 🔒 Deterministic Static Compiler
Rust owns discovery, catalog resolution, link checking, sitemaps, RSS/Atom feeds, and Markdown rendering. Content builds are byte-reproducible and lightning fast.

### 🎨 Custom `.rocci` Themes
Decouple static documentation prose from presentation templates. Custom themes written in `.rocci` define named layouts (`home`, `product`, `section`, `docs`, `news-index`, `news-post`, `plain`, `not-found`) with compile-time type checking.

### 📦 Typed Static Collections
Organize blogs, announcements, changelogs, and case studies into typed collections with deterministic date sorting, draft exclusion, and automated Atom feed generation.

### 🧩 Rich Semantic Components
Use built-in semantic documentation directives like `@docs tabs`, `@docs note`, `@docs figure`, and `@docs include` to build structured technical manuals without client JavaScript.

---

## Architecture at a Glance

```text
Rocci Ecosystem
├── Core: Application runtime, CLI, and .rocci template engine
└── Rocdown
    ├── .rocdown content format & parser
    ├── Content catalog & static site generator
    ├── Typed static collections & Atom feeds
    └── Project-local .rocci theme seam
```

---

## Syntax Showcase

### 1. Page Metadata Declaration
```markdown
@page {
    layout: "docs",
    published: "2026-08-18",
    authors: ["Rocci Team"],
    meta: {
        title: "Getting Started",
        description: "Orientation and first success with Rocci",
    },
}
```

### 2. Tabbed Code Panels (No JavaScript Required)
```markdown
@docs tabs {
    group: "install"
    kind: "tool"

    @docs tab {
        id: "cli"
        label: "CLI"
        Run the site check command:
        ```sh
        rocdown check site
        ```
    }

    @docs tab {
        id: "cargo"
        label: "Cargo"
        Run with cargo:
        ```sh
        cargo run -p rocci-rocdown-cli -- check site
        ```
    }
}
```

### 3. Semantic Callouts
```markdown
@docs note {
    title: "Important"
    kind: "important"

    Rocdown static builds verify every link at compile time.
}
```

